1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,385
The trillions of dollars flowing through artificial intelligence pass

2
00:00:04,385 --> 00:00:06,822
through twelve distinct layers —

3
00:00:06,822 --> 00:00:10,720
most of which you have never heard of.

4
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:15,481
Hyperscalers have already committed over five hundred billion dollars

5
00:00:15,481 --> 00:00:17,596
to AI infrastructure —

6
00:00:17,596 --> 00:00:20,770
and the build-out is only accelerating.

7
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:27,112
Almost the entire stack lives in just four countries:

8
00:00:27,112 --> 00:00:32,750
the United States, the Netherlands, Korea, and Taiwan.

9
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:40,168
From sand to software, twelve layers stack on top of each other.

10
00:00:40,168 --> 00:00:46,350
Each one is its own industry, with its own leaders.

11
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:51,600
Three single companies effectively control three layers.

12
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:55,350
ASML, NVIDIA, and SK Hynix.

13
00:00:55,350 --> 00:00:56,558
Take ASML.

14
00:00:56,558 --> 00:01:01,992
Their newest High-NA EUV machines cost four hundred million

15
00:01:01,992 --> 00:01:07,426
dollars each, and there is no alternative anywhere on

16
00:01:07,426 --> 00:01:08,030
Earth.

17
00:01:08,030 --> 00:01:12,260
Every prompt you type rides on a supply chain

18
00:01:12,260 --> 00:01:16,490
that begins in the Netherlands, passes through Taiwan and

19
00:01:16,490 --> 00:01:19,310
Korea, and ends in your browser.

20
00:01:19,310 --> 00:01:22,941
The next bottleneck is not chips.

21
00:01:22,941 --> 00:01:24,757
It is electricity.

22
00:01:24,757 --> 00:01:30,204
AI is pushing data centers toward consuming Japan's entire

23
00:01:30,204 --> 00:01:33,230
annual power supply by 2030.

24
00:01:33,230 --> 00:01:37,422
On top sits the visible part —

25
00:01:37,422 --> 00:01:41,614
the foundation labs you have heard of.

26
00:01:41,614 --> 00:01:44,010
Six contenders, one prize.

27
00:01:44,010 --> 00:01:50,767
Nine out of ten of these companies sit in just four countries.

28
00:01:50,767 --> 00:01:56,960
This boom is more concentrated than any gold rush in history.

29
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:57,469
Subscribe.

30
00:01:57,469 --> 00:02:02,053
Next episode, we go inside the Dutch monopoly that

31
00:02:02,053 --> 00:02:04,090
controls all of it.
